course: dictionary
lesson: 10512
title: One word, many twists
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word twist is a good example. Look at the words around it before you decide what it means.
explain: «An emergency stop button cuts the power at once and stays pressed in until someone has checked the problem and twisted it out.» Here twisted means turned to release the button. You know this because the button stays pressed in until it is twisted out, so the twist is a turning action.
explain: «Stories grow because people add a twist that makes the tale better to tell.» Here a twist is a noun, a surprise in a story. Try your meaning in the sentence: a surprise that makes the tale better fits, so the meaning is right.
explain: «A falling cat twists its front half one way and its back half the other.» Here twists means bends or turns something in a different direction. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? Turns or bends fits, so twist means that.
fact: Twist is a verb (twist, twists, twisted, twisting) and a noun (a twist, twists).
fact: To twist means to turn something round, like twisting a lid off a jar.
fact: To twist a joint means to hurt it by turning it the wrong way, as in «twist your ankle».
fact: A twist can be a surprising change in a story, as in «a twist in the tale».
fact: Phrases like «twists and turns» mean bends and curves, and «twist someone's arm» means to persuade them.
exercise: «She had to twist the lid to open the jar.» What does twist mean here? | To hit the lid hard | To paint the lid | To pull the lid off with a hard tug | *To turn something round
exercise: «He twisted his ankle on the stairs and had to rest it.» What happened to his ankle? | *He hurt it by turning it the wrong way | He tied it into a knot | He painted it | He washed it in a bath
exercise: «The ending of the book had a twist nobody expected.» What is a twist in a story? | A type of rope | *A sudden, surprising change | A long, boring list of facts | Another name for the first page
test: «Follow the twists and turns of the road.» What do twists and turns mean here? | *Bends and curves | Sudden stops | Loud noises | Straight lines
test: «She had to twist his arm to join the team.» What does twist his arm mean? | To tie his arm in a sling | *To persuade him | To break his arm | To measure his arm
exam: In «add a twist that makes the tale better to tell», what is a twist? | *A surprising change to the story | A piece of string | A tiny mistake in the spelling | A short rest before the end
